  "notes": "Derived from the revised AI-generated sheet, matching the supplied reference with requested edits. Automatically reduced grid interpretation; small details differ from the reference. Grip/pivot/muzzle are initial estimates requiring rig checks. Preview slot W04 confirmed from repository pixelkit-v2 manifest at ae7247a9b94aeb834342cd40e8aea2eb82308bb8. This does not add firing behaviours.\nRevision: weapons-v001. Status: draft. Pixel cleanup and anchor/scale review outstanding. Stored in isolated art/weapon-lab branch.\n\nWeapon-lighting-v001: Three amber charge pips roll forward; existing cyan status lights answer out of phase. 20 frames at 20 fps; 1s loop. Anchors, dimensions, body silhouette, scale, trim/guts unchanged. New lamp seats affect 3 body pixels inside the existing silhouette. Existing emissive colours preserved. Draft: in-game visibility and exact art approval pending. No geometry, articulated motion, firing trigger or 2x density changes.\n\nAnchor-alignment-v001: calibrated handle grip and muzzle for the enlarged weapon rig. Body and all animation layers unchanged. Runtime scales around the grip; ranged shots use the transformed muzzle. Scale remains 1.2. Pending alignment verification.\n\nArt Pass V2: material-family harmonisation. Eight-step neutral charcoal/gunmetal ramp derived from the generated V2 material reference. Original pixel geometry, alpha, markers, scale, dimensions, fps, frame count, emissive PNGs, trim and guts are unchanged. Every frame uses the same RGB material mapping. Existing cyan, magenta, red and amber light identities and all original loops retained. Source is the current shared build 20261101T094357Z-78228871. Saved draft; renderer comparison only; battle playtest and art approval pending.\nJarred: dark red metal magazine/receiver and pale red, nearly pink top light, using og.jpg as tone reference. Generated reference transferred to original 42×20 mask; no silhouette, grip/muzzle, scale or FPS/frame-count change. Existing staggered lamp envelope retained, top amber changed to pale pink; added low breathing pink rail within existing material silhouette. Draft, not released.\nRevision: previous broad red paint superseded. Dark neutral V2 metal restored, with only a slim oxblood magazine edge accent (about 3% or less of opaque material pixels). Piercing pale-pink rail and all 20 emissive PNG frames retained byte-for-byte from the pink-rail version. Original silhouette, dimensions, sockets, scale and cadence unchanged. This follows Jarred’s correction: dark gun, piercing rail, tiny red touch.",
